{
  "about": "§12 (docs/multisig-machines.md): the sign door over a review's state. A sign / propose / approve / execute button is enabled ONLY when the state is ready and the review's sign rule allows it; a missing state is loading. Replayed through the link door `review.door {state?, review?}` by Rust, the web, the desktop, Android and iOS. D1 (real-device pass 2): a ready review whose state-change check AND simulation both could not be read (its `unchecked` concern) is drawn, but the door asks for \"… anyway\" whatever its sign rule says and carries the danger line (`reason_key` home.multisig.review.state.unchecked) with Try again (`retry`); one check unread alone stays a plain caution. `checks` (replayed by Rust through `multisig_review`): the review's own rule, state guard × simulation — whatever left both unread: a hang (each read gave up at its bound), a refused connection (r13-2: ready in 2–4 s), or the reads right after Try again. A case's `trace` / `probe` / `sim` are the answers the review is gathered from (absent: an unreachable read, or for a read check the fixture's own). r14-13 (`settle`): where a gathered review lands, replayed through `review.settle {review?, answers}` — `answers` are the envelopes of every read the core made of the network ({result} / {error} / {unreachable}): the multisig's own code, the code rounds, the state trace and probe. A review whose network answered NONE of them is `failed {chainUnread}` — never signable, not even \"… anyway\", with Try again; one whose network answered (a node that says \"method not found\" answered) is `ready`, and the door decides \"… anyway\" when the two safety checks alone are unread. §18 (b) (`missing`): a proposal sheet opened WITHOUT a link whose transaction is not in the list, replayed through `review.missing {loading, unreadable, mailbox?}` → `{key, retry}` — a multisig service that did not answer is said as that with Try again, never \"it hasn't been shared with the members yet\". r16-3 (`recheck`): whether a gathered review's safety checks are FINAL for this read, replayed through `review.checksFinal {review?, anchor, checks, rechecked_ms}` → bool. `checks` are the envelopes of the state trace, the probe and the simulation. A review that would land unchecked (its `unchecked` concern) while its network answered its multisig's own state and any check is still silent is not final: those checks are asked again, paced, until one answers or the re-ask reaches its own limit (RECHECK_MS, 10 s); only then is \"unchecked\" (… anyway) published. A check the network refused (an {error}) is final for that check.",
  "timeout_ms": 40000,
  "keys": [
    "home.multisig.review.state.loading",
    "home.multisig.review.state.blocked",
    "home.multisig.review.state.timedOut",
    "home.multisig.review.state.unreadable",
    "home.multisig.review.state.gone",
    "home.multisig.review.state.tryAgain",
    "home.multisig.review.state.unchecked",
    "home.multisig.review.state.chainUnread"
  ],
  "door": [
